Z||000007||Formula88||12-28-2001||10:45 AM||||Are there any issues with the install, since it's a bit bigger then the OEM muffler?  Did you just have the muffler and tailpipes put on, or did you do any other exhaust piping?<P>I'm probably gonna re-do my entire exhaust system in the Spring, so I'm trying to get an idea what to look out for.  I'm thinking about the Spin Tech with WCF'c 2.5" exhaust system and hi-flow cat.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Voytek||12-28-2001||10:58 AM||||Where did you get one of those mufflers from and how much was it?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Smokin' GT||12-28-2001||03:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR>[B]Are there any issues with the install, since it's a bit bigger then the OEM muffler?  Did you just have the muffler and tailpipes put on, or did you do any other exhaust piping?<BR>B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, yes there is an issue, and that is that it eliminates the orignial spring mounts on the muffler itself.  At first my exhaust guy wasn't even going to do it because of that fact, but I called Chris at West Coast and then I called Fiero Store and the spin-tech as well as the ocelot eliminated the springs on the muffler and just used the tip mounts.<P>I only got the muffler and the tips, no change in pipe size, I didn't feel that it was incredibly necessary as I'm not going to be making this thing a race car or anything!<P>Voytek- I got the muffler from <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A>  (West Coast Fiero), it was aweseome quality and the sound is great.  It cost $108+ shipping<P><P>------------------<BR>-87 Bright Blue Metallic GT-<BR>          -Joel||||reg||1
